# Duration literals beyond machine integers

The components of a duration are machine integers: a literal number of days,
months or years that does not fit one is reported at the literal.

```catala
declaration scope S:
  output d content duration

scope S:
  definition d equals 99999999999999999999 day
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala typecheck
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  This number of days is too large for a duration, whose components are
│  machine integers.
│
├─➤ tests/date/bad/duration_literal_too_large.catala_en:11.23-47:
│    │
│ 11 │   definition d equals 99999999999999999999 day
│    │                       ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
└─ Duration literals beyond machine integers
#return code 123#
```
